//============================================================================================================================================
//                                                            SLATEUI.SYMBOLINDEX
//============================================================================================================================================
// 🧩 Symbol roll for SlateUI — Every ink and every measured extent the interface draws with — resolved once against the display scale, then read.

%format   symbolindex 1.0
%scope    layer
%path     Engine/SlateUI
%folders  16
%symbols  366

//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//                                                     FOLDER INDEXES
//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

I Api    | Api/Api.symbolindex       | 58 sym | Every ink and every measured extent the interface draws with — resolved once against the display scale, then read.
I Source | Source/Source.symbolindex | 2 sym  | Multiplies every declared extent by the display scale exactly once.
I Api    | Api/Api.symbolindex       | 41 sym | Two drawers over one display extent — their grab arbitration, their snap arbitration, their tongues and their interiors.
I Source | Source/Source.symbolindex | 40 sym | Grab arbitration, elastic constraint, the two snap arbitrations, and the clipped tongue.
I Api    | Api/Api.symbolindex       | 9 sym  | One pointer contact resolved into a phase, a travel since arrival, a smoothed rate and a tap verdict.
I Source | Source/Source.symbolindex | 5 sym  | The contact phase machine — one edge per tick, one accumulation, one smoothed rate.
I Api    | Api/Api.symbolindex       | 46 sym | The one seam the interface library crosses — device handles in, recorded commands out, no ImGui spelling.
I Source | Source/Source.symbolindex | 39 sym | The only translation unit in the engine that includes ImGui.
I Api    | Api/Api.symbolindex       | 18 sym | Time-sampled interpolants that retire themselves — and report, once per tick, whether anything still moves.
I Source | Source/Source.symbolindex | 22 sym | A semi-implicit spring, a Newton-solved cubic ease, and the one sweep that retires both.
I Api    | Api/Api.symbolindex       | 16 sym | Three marks of rising cost, and the one question a tick asks before it presents anything at all.
I Source | Source/Source.symbolindex | 12 sym | A flat enrolment of marks, and the three-operand wake rule read from it.
I Api    | Api/Api.symbolindex       | 13 sym | Stroke figures declared in a 24-unit square, enrolled by discipline — no raster, no store, no vendor library.
I Source | Source/Source.symbolindex | 6 sym  | The seven declared figures, transcribed from the source's own path data, plus the mark everything else draws as.
I Api    | Api/Api.symbolindex       | 20 sym | One tick of the interface — springs, drawers, and the assembled recording, shared by every host.
I Source | Source/Source.symbolindex | 19 sym | The shared tick driver — springs, drawers, and the assembled recording.

