T PointerCondition                      | Api/RecordingSurface.h             | 68-79   | What the pointer did between the previous tick and this one. `InputExchange`. The two observe the same device through two surfaces that never merge: the stroke path needs arrival stamps at device rate, the interface needs one resolved position per tick, and merging them would give the canvas the interface's rate.
T DisplayCondition                      | Api/RecordingSurface.h             | 83-89   | What the display reported for this tick.
T RecordingSurface                      | Api/RecordingSurface.h             | 104-262 | Records the interface's own primitives into the open interface tick. source file. `00` §2.2 makes a **host** including `imgui.h` a defect; it does not forbid a second unit inside `SlateUI`, which already owns the one copy. The alternative was recording panels through built-in widgets, and no built-in widget produces a clipped tongue, an eight-pixel glow, a scrim or tracked small capitals — the four things the source is mostly made of. window writes into content nothing will assemble.
